/* Aarhus — sample style.css
 *
 * The theme already covers everything a Theming Center setting can express:
 * the palette (`brand_color`, `text_color`, `heading_color`, `link_color`,
 * `hover_link_color`, `background_color`), the fonts, the 1300px shell, the
 * article card with its 260px sidebar card, the responsive stacking below
 * 1024px, rich text tables, figures and captions, and the code blocks (copy
 * button, language badge, 24rem cap).
 *
 * What is left is the last mile: rules that describe *your* content and have
 * no setting behind them. Upload this file through *Custom settings → Inject
 * style* (rename it to `style.css` first) or paste the rules into the theme's
 * own `style.css`.
 *
 * The four examples are independent — keep the ones you need.
 */

/* 1. Content convention: the bold lead-in of a list item is a warning.
      The selectors are scoped to the rich text containers, so the same markup
      in menus, buttons or the sidebar is not affected. */
.article-body ul li strong,
.post-body ul li strong {
  color: #CC3340;
}

/* 2. Printing an article. The theme already un-caps and un-scrolls code blocks
      and hides the copy button when printing; hide the furniture around the
      text as well and flatten the cards. */
@media print {
  .header,
  .sub-nav,
  .footer,
  .article-sidebar,
  .article-footer,
  .article-relatives,
  .article-votes,
  .share {
    display: none !important;
  }

  .article {
    background-color: transparent !important;
    border-radius: 0 !important;
    margin: 0 !important;
    padding: 0 !important;
  }
}

/* 3. A shorter code cap on phones. `--code-block-max-height` is the documented
      hook (theme default: 24rem); the theme reads it as a custom property, so
      no `!important` is needed. */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .code-block {
    --code-block-max-height: 16rem;
  }
}

/* 4. Your own components. The rich text editor keeps the classes you type in
      its HTML view, so a callout is one rule away. */
.callout {
  background-color: #F1F5F9;
  border-left: 4px solid #007ACC;
  border-radius: 5px;
  margin: 0 0 20px;
  padding: 16px 20px;
}

.callout > :last-child {
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

/* What this file is *not* for: hiding whole blocks (article votes, sharing,
 * comments, the section sidebar). The **Article page elements** settings
 * remove the markup instead, which leaves no empty borders or spacing behind —
 * see docs/customization.md#article-page-elements.
 *
 * Tip: rules pasted into the theme's own `style.css` may keep the Sass
 * variables that file already uses (`$link_color`, `$primary-shade`, …); an
 * uploaded file is plain CSS and needs literal values. */
